Build the warning message first, then pass it to `format_with_border`. Your function will ignore ANSI codes when calculating the padding and add both borders automatically.

```rust
let syntax = ps
    .find_syntax_by_token(language)
    .or_else(|| ps.find_syntax_by_name(language))
    .unwrap_or_else(|| {
        let warning = format!(
            "  \x1b[1;33mWarning\x1b[0m: syntax highlighting not available for {} using plain text",
            language
        );

        println!("{}", format_with_border(&warning, width));

        ps.find_syntax_plain_text()
    });
```

Here, `width` is the **space inside the borders**, not the total line width. Use the same value as your other bordered lines to keep them aligned.

Note that `saturating_sub` prevents underflow but does not truncate: if the warning is longer than `width`, the right border will extend beyond the intended position.

